LKGeek KernelSU compatibility overlay
====================================

Upstream source remains the pristine KernelSU submodule, pinned to
ReSukiSU/ReSukiSU d7260ca1e5c128061122924d0d48754e361e135c.
Its current project name is BakaSU. Initialize it with git submodule update
--init KernelSU before building. Do not edit the upstream checkout.

This directory replaces the former single symlink with links to upstream
files/directories and three small source overlays:

* Kbuild: resolves metadata from the real submodule and selects our reviewed
  SUSFS 2.1/4.19 compatibility checks instead of upstream's blanket SUSFS stop.
  All upstream inline-hook, API and symbol checks remain enabled.
* feature/sucompat.c and .h: keep the user-path stat/access ABI on kernels
  below 5.0; the rest of these files is the pinned upstream code.
* susfs_compat.mk: preserves upstream feature detection and requires the
  kernel-side SUSFS_BAKASU_LEGACY_COMPAT contract.

The kernel-side contract adds NO_SU and zygote-next task flags, deferred
sus-path refresh work, and a post-exec callback to install the scoped su
session descriptor. The exec marker is consumed on success and cleared on
failure. SELinux symbols needed by the new feature are visible to built-in
KSU without requiring DEBUG_KERNEL/KALLSYMS_ALL.

On future upstream upgrades, refresh the three copied files from the new
pin and reapply/review these differences; add any new feature-file links.
Check every symlink and rerun the Wayne build and KSU_TEST=1 VM suite.
This overlay is a local legacy adaptation, not a claim of upstream SUSFS
support or Android/device-level root validation.
